 {
-  "id": "grammar.b2.brasilsudeste.03.brasil-voz-media-pronominal",
-  "title": "Pronominal Middle Voice in Aesthetic Analysis",
+  "id": "grammar.b2.brasilsudeste.03.se",
+  "title": "The 1922 Modern Art Week: Which Se?",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "En la crítica artística e histórica sobre el modernismo brasileño, la voz media pronominal presenta un proceso que afecta al sujeto de forma espontánea o interna, sin que se perciba una acción impuesta por un agente exterior."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know the different jobs of *se* from B2 Unit 19: reflexive, reciprocal, passive, impersonal and accidental. A text about an art movement uses several of them in a few lines, so it is a good place to ask \"who does what to whom?\" Here they work on the Modern Art Week of 1922."
     },
     {
       "type": "table",
-      "title": "Estructuras de voz media pronominal",
+      "title": "Five kinds of se, in São Paulo, 1922",
       "rows": [
         [
-          "La estética académica se disolvió ante la audacia de los pintores modernistas.",
-          "Academic aesthetics dissolved before the boldness of modernist painters."
+          "Reflexive: someone does it to themselves",
+          "Los jóvenes artistas se presentaron ante el público. (presented themselves)"
         ],
         [
-          "El canon artístico se transformó con la irrupción de las vanguardias paulistas.",
-          "The artistic canon transformed with the irruption of the Paulista avant-garde."
+          "Reciprocal: two or more do it to each other",
+          "Los modernistas se conocían y se escribían cartas. (wrote to each other)"
         ],
         [
-          "La identidad nacional brasileña se forjó asimilando múltiples raíces culturales.",
-          "Brazilian national identity was forged by assimilating multiple cultural roots."
+          "Passive: a thing, no doer named",
+          "En 1922 se celebró la Semana de Arte Moderna. (was held)"
         ],
         [
-          "Las formas tradicionales se quebraron durante la Semana de Arte Moderno de 1922.",
-          "Traditional forms broke apart during the Modern Art Week of 1922."
+          "Impersonal: nobody in particular",
+          "Se dice que el público abucheó a los artistas. (it is said)"
+        ],
+        [
+          "Accidental: se + me, te, le, nos",
+          "Se me perdió el programa de la exposición. (I lost the programme)"
         ]
       ]
     },
+    {
+      "type": "examples",
+      "title": "Same word, different jobs",
+      "items": [
+        {
+          "spanish": "Se leyeron poemas y se presentaron cuadros durante tres noches.",
+          "english": "Poems were read and paintings were shown over three nights."
+        },
+        {
+          "spanish": "Oswald y Tarsila se admiraban mucho.",
+          "english": "Oswald and Tarsila admired each other a lot."
+        },
+        {
+          "spanish": "Se nos olvidó el catálogo en casa.",
+          "english": "We forgot the catalogue at home."
+        }
+      ]
+    },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Diferencia sutil: en 'la estética se disolvió' el verbo denota un cambio de estado interno (voz media), no una acción refleja donde el sujeto actúa sobre sí mismo como agente voluntario."
+      "content": "Ask what the noun does. If *se* + a plural thing agrees with the verb (*se leyeron poemas*), it is passive. If nobody is named and there is no noun (*se dice que*), it is impersonal. If *me, te, le, nos* follows *se* and the verb agrees with the thing (*se me perdió el programa*), it is accidental."
     }
   ]
-}
